# Shell scripts must check out with LF endings on every machine.
#
# This repo is worked from Windows laptops where git's core.autocrlf is true.
# Without this rule, .claude/hooks/*.sh checks out with CRLF and bash fails at
# the shebang with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" — so the very hook
# meant to warn a second machine that it is behind would not run there.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Generated brand assets that scripts/__tests__/brand-icons.test.ts compares
# byte for byte with what scripts/brand-icons.mjs writes (LF). With autocrlf
# on Windows, app/icon.svg checked out with CRLF and the test failed (#88).
app/icon.svg text eol=lf
